# Riffle repo-data-extractor — environment
# This file is loaded automatically; you do NOT need to set anything in the shell.
# Fill in your values after the '=' (no quotes needed). Keep this file private —
# it is gitignored so your token is never committed.

# GitHub personal access token (read scope: public_repo, or repo for private).
# Used for: PR list, CI-check results, labels, and the GHSA vulnerability check.
# Without it you get 60 requests/hour and no labels. Format: ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxx
GITHUB_TOKEN=TOKEN

# LLM semantic flags (Source 6), on by default (turn off with --no-llm).
# The default backend is headless Claude Code (`claude -p`, your own login): no key needed.
# LLM_API_KEY is only for LLM_BACKEND=api: an ANTHROPIC API key, called through Anthropic's
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint via the openai SDK (pip install openai).
LLM_API_KEY=KEY

LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# python build_dataset.py --max-prs 9 --llm --declared-labels --szz --ci-history --out dataset_9pr.parquet
# Team store (optional, ADR 0015). Both set: the miner sends its logs, health files, dataset and
# shard manifest after each repo, on a Stop and at the end. ci_cache/ never leaves this PC.
# The lead gives you the URL and a token for this PC. Unset: nothing is sent.
RIFFLE_SYNC_URL=
RIFFLE_SYNC_TOKEN=
# Easier: `python join.py CODE` fills in the two lines above from the code the lead sends you.
# Lead only, to hand out tokens with --shard-plan N --issue-tokens (never share it):
# RIFFLE_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# A read token (rd_…) for the store's pages; `python doctor.py` saves it, the TUI's F4 copies it and opens the page:
# RIFFLE_READ_TOKEN=
